WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.080
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:05.029
For most of us, when we’re people watching,
the normal thoughts that come into our heads

00:00:05.029 --> 00:00:06.441
are “I wonder where they’re going?”

00:00:06.441 --> 00:00:10.769
“Is that a couple” “Are they wearing
those clothes for a dare?”

00:00:10.769 --> 00:00:15.629
But there are a select few of us whose first
thought, when they spot a face in the crowd,

00:00:15.629 --> 00:00:18.439
is “mustard or gravy?”

00:00:18.439 --> 00:00:24.180
Human meat, the great forbidden delicacy,
has been eaten throughout history because

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:30.580
of rituals, desperate bids for survival, curiosity
and when Tesco ran out of horse meat.

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:35.540
Cannibalism, or anthropophagy as it’s officially
known, is still occasionally practiced in

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:40.450
places like Indonesian New Guinea, but has
generally been the last resort of those with

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:45.550
no other choice, like when stuck up a mountain,
adrift on the ocean or locked in a KFC.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:47.540
So where does the law stand on this?

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:52.750
And how about your doctor, how would he feel
about you literally taking your pound of flesh?

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:57.340
Today we find out; can you eat people?

00:00:57.340 --> 00:01:05.170
In most parts of the world, there has been
a strong disdain for cannibalism, which you

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:10.330
can see reflected in the myths and folklore
where it’s used an example of truly depraved

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:15.380
behavior, such as in Hansel and Gretel and
stories of the witch Baba Yaga.

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:21.580
In Greek mythology, Tantalus was punished
for boiling up his son, Pelops, and serving

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:22.990
him to the gods.

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:28.381
He was sent to the deepest corner of the underworld
and his fitting castigation was that when

00:01:28.381 --> 00:01:33.340
he was hungry and grasped for a grape, it
was always just too high.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:38.450
And the water below him also shrunk away whenever
he tried to quench his thirst.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:45.050
This is where we get the word “tantalizing”;
something that is just out of reach.

00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:49.850
For those tribes that did indulge in the practice
of cannibalism, it was either to absorb the

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:55.370
power of those they had killed, such as the
strength of rival warriors, or it was a process

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:59.430
of grieving and would be done to the bodies
of friends and family members.

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:03.600
I’m assuming the flowers were used as some
sort of side salad.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:09.340
Many sieges throughout history, such as Jerusalem
in 70AD and the First Crusades, have reports

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:15.360
of soldiers and civilians having to cannibalize
the fallen when all other supplies were exhausted.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:23.230
In World War 2, during the 872-day assault
on Leningrad, now St Petersburg, the police

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:27.760
had to form an anti-cannibalism division,
which was only slightly more popular than

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:28.760
traffic duty.

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:31.410
Well, would you want to give a ticket to a
tank?

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:37.540
Of course, human beings are not alone in this
merry sport, there are plenty of animal species

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:42.570
who will happily chew their way through the
odd cousin, such as the usually vegetarian

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:48.959
hippos who were found chomping on a decaying
hippo carcasses during a difficult year.

00:02:48.959 --> 00:02:54.959
But for some species, especially at the early
stage of development, cannibalism is programmed

00:02:54.959 --> 00:03:00.590
to kick in depending on the environment, as
a form of species preservation.

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:04.770
When tiger salamanders are born, if there’s
not too many larvae then they all develop

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:09.620
nice and friendly and remember to buy each
other socks for Christmas.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:13.970
But at some point, when it all gets a bit
overcrowded, then a random selection start

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:19.510
growing with a broader head and triple length
teeth and, rather than chasing the normal

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:25.830
dinner of aquatic invertebrates, they devour
the smaller salamanders who are the most nutritious

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:27.319
available meal.

00:03:27.319 --> 00:03:34.050
It’s cannibal coding to make sure that at
least some of the offspring survive when there’s

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:35.560
not enough food to go round.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:39.890
It’s a bit like a mother of five throwing
two cheeseburgers into the kitchen and then

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:41.300
locking all the doors.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:44.379
Ignore the screaming; it’s for their own
good.

00:03:44.379 --> 00:03:49.810
And if you think that’s mean of mum, well
nature has its own revenge planned there.

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:55.340
If you didn’t think spiders were already
awful enough, the crab spider mother lays

00:03:55.340 --> 00:04:03.560
extra unfertilized eggs for her young to eat
but, greedy-sideways-walking-sticky-string-spewing-agents-of-satan

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:10.000
that they are, it’s not enough and they
also eat their own mother over a few weeks.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:13.069
Honestly, this generation, no respect.

00:04:13.069 --> 00:04:19.560
This is called Matriphagy, which means “mother-eating”
and… well, you just go ahead and make your

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:20.819
own joke.

00:04:20.819 --> 00:04:22.300
So, back to humans.

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:27.350
Unlike these salamanders and spider, us humans
are clearly not genetically designed to eat

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:30.740
our own flesh so; is it safe?

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:35.410
In the 1930s, Australian gold prospectors
discovered there was a huge population of

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:41.169
native people living in the highlands of Papa
New Guinea, an area we had thought to be relatively

00:04:41.169 --> 00:04:42.460
empty before then.

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:46.480
Over the next few decades, as researchers
began to spend time with these people, they

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:52.389
found there was a very mysterious disease
that was killing around 200 a year in the

00:04:52.389 --> 00:04:55.870
eleven thousand strong Fore tribe.

00:04:55.870 --> 00:05:02.060
It was known as Kuru, which meant “trembling”,
since sufferers would quickly lose control

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:04.710
over their limbs, as well as their emotions.

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:10.310
Once it took hold, it took about a year before
they were completely incapacitated.

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:14.169
The obvious suspicion was that it was some
rare genetic condition that had been passed

00:05:14.169 --> 00:05:17.240
down within the small DNA pool of the tribe.

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:23.610
But as they tracked the victims, they realized
that there was a correlation with social groups

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:30.150
but not with genetic ones, so there must be
an environmental reason.

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:32.599
And of course you have already guessed what
it was.

00:05:32.599 --> 00:05:37.379
The Fore believed it was better that they
ate their dead than leave it as food for the

00:05:37.379 --> 00:05:43.189
worms so they whipped up a cranial stew of
brain, fern and bamboo, while the rest of

00:05:43.189 --> 00:05:45.169
the body was roasted over the fire.

00:05:45.169 --> 00:05:50.199
It’s thought that at some point, one of
the Fore must have developed CJD, Creutzfeldt-Jakob

00:05:50.199 --> 00:05:55.090
Disease, the human form of mad cow disease,
and then that was spread through the tribe,

00:05:55.090 --> 00:06:01.042
not as a virus or bacteria but by eating the
brain prions, which is a messed up kind of

00:06:01.042 --> 00:06:07.840
protein, which could take decades to take
hold and begin the mysterious Kuru.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:13.400
So, from a doctor’s point of view, eating
humans is probably up there with smoking,

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:17.580
drinking super-sized sodas and that thing
you do when the door’s closed; it makes

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:19.539
you go blind apparently.

00:06:19.539 --> 00:06:23.419
Doctors is one thing but what about lawyers?

00:06:23.419 --> 00:06:25.590
Do they enjoy the taste of human…

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:31.340
I mean… is it, from a legal perspective,
okay to consume another person?

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:34.960
Obviously, killing people is off the table,
that is almost certainly illegal.

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:39.559
But can you take a nibble on a corpse if you
come across it in the forest?

00:06:39.559 --> 00:06:42.129
And what about in the case of desperation?

00:06:42.129 --> 00:06:48.499
Much of the ruling that exists is built around
a law school classic called Regina versus

00:06:48.499 --> 00:06:53.229
Dudley and Stephens from 1884, with Regina
being Queen Victoria, at this point.

00:06:53.229 --> 00:06:58.389
A ship called the Mignonette (“Min-yon-ay”)
was sailing from Southampton to Sydney when

00:06:58.389 --> 00:07:03.259
it hit a gale near the Cape of Good Hope and
they had to abandon ship, ending up in a lifeboat

00:07:03.259 --> 00:07:06.970
with just some navigation equipment and two
tins of turnips.

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:14.319
There were 4 people in total, the captain
Tom Dudley, two sailors Edwin Stephens and

00:07:14.319 --> 00:07:20.279
Edmund Brooks, and a 17 year old cabin boy
named Richard Parker.

00:07:20.279 --> 00:07:22.592
After two days, they ate the first tin of
turnips.

00:07:22.592 --> 00:07:25.539
I’m sure it was delicious.

00:07:25.539 --> 00:07:29.990
A couple of days later they managed to kill
a turtle and this, along with the other turnip

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:34.149
tin, let them survive to almost 2 weeks at
sea.

00:07:34.149 --> 00:07:39.110
Richard Parker fell very ill and slipped into
a probable coma.

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:44.120
After much discussion and almost 20 days in
the life boat, Dudley pushed his penknife

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:47.999
into the boy’s neck, while Stephens held
his legs.

00:07:47.999 --> 00:07:52.629
Both claimed Brooks had agreed, but he denied
this.

00:07:52.629 --> 00:07:57.460
They all ate the dead boy and four or five
days later they were rescued.

00:07:57.460 --> 00:08:03.559
They told the truth when brought back to England
and a major case ensued, with Brooks turning

00:08:03.559 --> 00:08:05.020
state’s witness.

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:10.189
Both Dudley and Stephens were found guilty
of murder and sentenced to death, although

00:08:10.189 --> 00:08:14.669
they were eventually released after 6 months
in prison, thanks to the Home Secretary, William

00:08:14.669 --> 00:08:15.969
Harcourt.

00:08:15.969 --> 00:08:22.789
So killing for food in case of emergency is
not okay, but what about cannibalism without

00:08:22.789 --> 00:08:24.550
the killing part?

00:08:24.550 --> 00:08:29.490
Canadian artist Rick Gibson, obviously having
run out of paint and canvasses, decided to

00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:34.120
eat the flesh of another person in public,
in 1988.

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:41.169
He ate a canape made of donated tonsils in
London and the UK has no specific law against

00:08:41.169 --> 00:08:42.169
it.

00:08:42.169 --> 00:08:47.130
The next year, he set the bar even lower when
he ate a human testicle.

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:53.330
When he tried the same thing in Vancouver,
they confiscated his snack and charged him

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:59.040
with “publicly exhibiting a disgusting object”
but the case was dropped and, having waited

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:04.690
almost 2 months, he hungrily finished his
lunch on the courthouse steps, after the verdict.

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:06.280
The media went nuts…

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:09.370
I mean, they had a ball…oh never mind.

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:15.300
All in all, it’s a good thing the social
taboo and medical dangers have kept us from

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:17.350
snacking on our friends and family.

00:09:17.350 --> 00:09:22.280
But, to keep temptation at a minimum, make
sure you never sit too near the fire and maybe

00:09:22.280 --> 00:09:31.280
rethink that bacon and maple syrup deodorant,
you’re just asking for trouble.

00:09:31.280 --> 00:09:48.640
Thanks for the view, subscribe for more Thoughty2.

